Restore the lost CD failure branch in Init_Application (dd2h.exe 0x412950).
At 0x412a51 the original calls FUN_00416094, tests EAX at 0x412a56 and
branches past the dialog only when nonzero. The failure path 0x412a5a-0x412a76
calls MessageBoxA(hwnd,0x46c5b0,0x46c5a4,MB_ICONERROR) then returns zero.
The strings in the original image are "Destruction Derby 2 CD Required" and
"FATAL ERROR". Ghidra dropped this path and ignored the initializer's result.
The real MCI backend and patch 836 now make CD_Check's 19-track test possible.
Propagate application-init failure out of the WASM CRT-bypass launcher too;
the native launcher performs the same result check. No engine bypass, fabricated
CD count or successful boot with unavailable audio tracks.

